    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">We are pleased to confirm the speakers for our webinar <strong>Inclusive Elections: Ensuring the Right to Vote for All</strong>, on <strong>Tuesday, 27 October 2026 at 14:00&ndash;15:30 UTC</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 24px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">The session is about practice rather than law: what Election Management Bodies (EMBs) can do in polling places, in voter information and in staff training so that voters with disabilities, older voters, linguistic minorities, displaced people and rural communities can cast their ballot independently and in secret.</p>

    <!-- Speakers box -->
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin: 0 0 28px; background-color:#f0f4f8; border-radius:6px; border-left:4px solid #1a2744;">
    <tr><td style="padding: 20px 24px;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px; color:#1a2744; font-size:16px; font-weight:700;">Confirmed Speakers</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#1a2744; font-size:15px; font-weight:700;">Whitney Quesenbery</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#555; font-size:14px;">Chief Program Officer, Center for Civic Design</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">Helped write the usability and accessibility requirements for US voting systems, and works with election offices on ballots, voter information and polling places designed around the voter.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#1a2744; font-size:15px; font-weight:700;">Virginia Atkinson</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#555; font-size:14px;">Senior Global Advisor, Inclusion, International Foundation for Electoral Systems (IFES)</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">Lead author of IFES&rsquo;s <em>Equal Access</em> manual on including persons with disabilities in elections, and led the development of ElectionAccess.org.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#1a2744; font-size:15px; font-weight:700;">Colleen Roberts</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#555; font-size:14px;">Global Technical Lead, Inclusive Citizenship, Sightsavers</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">Works with electoral bodies and disability organisations in Cameroon, Senegal, Tanzania and Bangladesh on polling station accessibility and accessible voter education.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#1a2744; font-size:15px; font-weight:700;">Inge Volleberg</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 4px; color:#555; font-size:14px;">Researcher and Coordinator, Inclusion Europe</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5;">Inclusion Europe represents people with intellectual disabilities and their families, and campaigns for accessible elections and for the voting rights of people under guardianship.</p>
        <p style="margin:0; color:#555; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; font-style:italic;">A fifth speaker, from an electoral commission in the Southern African Development Community (SADC), will be confirmed shortly.</p>
    </td></tr>
